			},
			"28": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": false
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "EXAMPLE 2: REORDERING A COLLECTION\n\nIn this example we have a collection of Rectangle shapes in various sizes.\nThe rectangles get placed in a circle pattern.\nAt the bottom of the example we are using Split and Join to reorder the collection\nWe've added a switch so you can toggle between the original pattern and the reordered one.\n\nFor most reordering you can use nodes like Read\/Write\/Span\/Sort\/Shuffle\/Shift, but manually splitting and joining can sometimes be the solution to specific cases."
					}
				},
